cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Piazzi in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Piazzi: open source astrometry of asteroids and comets"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Perner
    given-names: Louis
version: 0.2.1
date-released: "2026-11-06"
license: MIT
url: "https://datamonkeys.ai/piazzi/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/datamonkeys-ai/piazzi"
keywords:
  - astrometry
  - asteroids
  - comets
  - minor planets
  - Gaia DR3
  - ADES
abstract: >-
  Piazzi finds moving objects in CCD images, solves the plate against Gaia DR3,
  measures positions and magnitudes with calibrated uncertainties, identifies
  known bodies and writes ADES/MPC reports. Accuracy is benchmarked against
  JPL Horizons on public ZTF and SDSS data.
